Three things were needed to make the suite trustworthy rather than merely green:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- **Stale-[38;5;10m.so[0m guard.** [38;5;10mcargo test[0m does not rebuild a [38;5;10mcdylib[0m that no Rust target links against. Early runs silently tested an old binary. The harness now compares [38;5;10m.so[0m mtime against [38;5;10msrc/**/*.rs[0m and fails loudly.[0m[0m
- **Global-state lock.** cJSON keeps process-wide state ([38;5;10mglobal_error[0m, [38;5;10mglobal_hooks[0m); parallel [38;5;10m#[test][0m threads interleaved it and produced spurious diffs. Every test holds a shared mutex, and parse observations interleave the C and Rust calls on the same buffer so error-pointer offsets are directly comparable.[0m[0m
- **Allocation-failure injection.** Rather than leaving the ~16 [38;5;10m(alloc)[0m error rows to inspection, a hook allocator fails the k-th request. This asserts C and Rust perform the [3msame number[23m of allocations across 17 operations (they do — e.g. Parse 14, Duplicate 26, Print 16) and then compares the outcome of forcing each one to fail.[0m[0m
